<p>During the Christmas holidays in December 2018, I visited Spain and spent two weeks travelling along the coastal cities.</p>

<p>I started my journey in Barcelona, where I spent two days which also included a day trip to Girona — a small town that recently gained traction for being a shooting location for the Game of Thrones series. From Barcelona I took a train along the coast to Valencia, and after soaking up its splendour I visited a small historical town called Cartagena, and then made my way to the beach town of Almería. I imagined the south of Spain to be warmer than the north, but was surprised to find snow on the mountain tops near Granada.</p>

